&Q000555 = Letter from Šarrum-bàni to Šu-Suen about keeping the Martu at bay
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.1.15
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.1.15&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. {d}šu-{d}suen lugal-ŋu₁₀-ra u₃-na-a-dug₄
#tr.en: Say to @wRN{Šu-@wDN{Suen}}, my lord: this is what @wPN{Šarrum-bāni},
#lem: Šusuen[1]RN; lugal[king]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. šar-ru-um-ba-ni gal-zu unken-na arad-zu na-ab-be₂-a
#tr.en: the 'Sage of the Assembly', your servant, says:
#lem: Šarrumbani[1]PN; galanzu[wise]; unkin[assembly]; arad[slave]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. bad₃ gal mu-ri-iq-tidnim-e dim₂-me-de₃ kiŋ₂-gi₄-a-aš bi₂-gi₄
#tr.en: You sent me a message ordering me to work on the construction of the great fortification @wGN{Murīq-Tidnim}.
#lem: bad[wall]; gal[big]; Muriqtidnim[1]; dim[create]; kiŋgia[messenger]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. (1:igi-zu mu-e-ŋar-ma:1)
#tr.en: @varh[t3115.v1]{You presented yourself before me } @vart[t3115.v2,t3115.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} A messenger presented himself before me }, announcing: @q[messenger,Carrum-bani]{“The @wEN{Martu} have invaded the land.”}
#lem: igi[eye]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=4

:4v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) igi-ni ma-an-ŋar-ma
#lem: igi[eye]; ŋar[put]

5. mar-tu ma-da-aš mu-un-šub-šub-bu-uš
#tr.en: @varh[t3115.v3]{You instructed me } @vart[t3115.v4,t3115.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} You have imposed on me as a task (?) } to build the fortification,
#lem: Martu[1 Amorite]; mada[land]; šub[fall]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. bad₃ du₃-u₃-de₃ ŋiri₃-bi ku₅-ru-de₃
#tr.en: so as to cut off their route;
#lem: bad[wall]; du[build]; ŋiri[foot]; kud[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. {id₂}idigna {id₂}buranuna-bi-da
#tr.en: also,
#lem: Idigna[1 Tigris]; Buranun[1 Euphrates]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. gu₂-ŋiri₃-bi a-šag₄-e nam-ba-e-šu₂-šu₂ (1:a₂-še₃:1) mu-e-da-aŋ₂
#tr.en: that no breaches of the @wWN{Tigris} or the @wWN{Euphrates} should cover the fields with water.
#lem: guŋiri[breach]; ašag[field]; šuš[cover]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]
#etcsl: line-id=8

:8v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) kiŋ₂-še₃
#lem: kiŋ[work]

9. zi-zi-da-ŋu₁₀-ne
#tr.en: When I was setting out,
#lem: zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. gu₂ {id₂}ab₂-gal-ta en-na ma-da zi-mu-dar{ki}-ra-še₃
#tr.en: their …… from the
#lem: gu[neck]; Abgal[1]WN; enna[until]; mada[land]; Zimudar[1]GN
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. [...]-bi i₃-zig₃-NE
#tr.en: bank of the @wWN{Ab-gal} watercourse to the province of @wGN{Zimudar}.
#lem: X; zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. bad₃-bi 26 danna-am₃ dim₂-e-da-ŋu₁₀-ne
#tr.en: When I was constructing this fortification to the length of 26 @fsux{danna},
#lem: bad[wall]; n; dana[unit of length]; dim[create]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. dal-ba-na hur-saŋ min-a-bi-ka sa₂ di-da-ŋu₁₀-ne
#tr.en: and had reached the area between the two mountain ranges,
#lem: dalbana[intermediate space or area]; hursaŋ[mountain]; n; sa[equal]; di[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. dim₂-me-ŋu₁₀-še₃ mar-tu hur-saŋ-ga-ka ib₂-tuš-a ŋeštug₂ mu-ši-in-ak
#tr.en: I was informed of the @wEN{Martu} camping within the mountain ranges because (?) of my building work.
#lem: dim[create]; Martu[1 Amorite]; hursaŋ[mountain]; tuš[sit (down)]; ŋeštug[ear]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. si-mu-ur₄{ki} nam-tab-ba-ni-še₃ im-ma-da-ŋen#
#tr.en: @wSN{Simurrum} had come to their assistance.
#lem: Simurrum[1]SN; namtab[partnership]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. dal-ba-na hur-saŋ ebih{ki}-ke₄ {ŋiš}tukul sag₃-ge-de₃ im-ma-ši-ŋen
#tr.en: So I set off to the area between the mountain ranges of @wGN{Ebiḫ} in order to engage in military action.
#lem: dalbana[intermediate space or area]; hursaŋ[mountain]; Ebih[1]GN; tukul[weapon]; sag[strike]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. u₃ ŋe₂₆-e erin₂ {gi}dusu i₃-il₂-il₂-eš-am₃ igi# nu#-um-mi-du₈
#tr.en: But as far as I can say, I have not seen (?) troops carrying baskets.
#lem: u[and]; ŋaʾe[I]; erin[people]; dupsik[basket (for carrying earth and bricks)]; il[raise]; igi[eye]; du[spread]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. {ŋiš}tukul sag₃-ge-de₃ X-ri-ni-še₃ ba-ŋen-na#
#tr.en: In order to engage in military action, I went (?) to their …….
#lem: tukul[weapon]; sag[strike]; X; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. tukum-bi lugal-ŋa₂ an-na-kam
#tr.en: If my lord agrees,
#lem: tukumbi[if]; lugal[king]; anna[approval]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. lu₂ kiŋ₂ ak-ne ha-ma-ab-tah-e a₂ ha-ma-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#tr.en: may he provide me with additional workmen and set the wages (?) for me.
#lem: lu[person]; kiŋ[work]; ak[do]; tah[add]; a[arm]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. gun₃-a ma-da sa₂ nu-ub-da-dug₄-ga dug₄-en-de₃-en
#tr.en: …… did not succeed …… tribute of the provinces (?).
#lem: gunu[speckled]; mada[land]; sa[equal]; dug[speak]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. ma-da MURUB₄{ki}-še₃ lu₂-kiŋ₂-gi₄-a mu-ni-gi₄
#tr.en: I sent a messenger to the province of @wGN{Murub}: the attitude (?) of the province has altered.
#lem: mada[land]; MURUB[1]GN; kiŋgia[messenger]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. ma-da dim₂-ma-bi ba-da-kur₂
#tr.en: I will not neglect to build the fortification -- in fact I am building and engaging in military action at the same time.
#lem: mada[land]; dimma[thought]; kur[different]
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. bad₃ du₃-u₃-de₃ nu-šub-be₂-en i₃-du₃-en u₃ {ŋiš}tukul i₃-sag₃-ge-en
#tr.en: After all,
#lem: bad[wall]; du[build]; šub[fall]; du[build]; u[and]; tukul[weapon]; sag[strike]
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. gal-zu unken-na im-ri-a gu-la-am₃ he₂-em-ma-da-ri
#tr.en: as 'Sage of the Assembly' I descend (?) from a great lineage!
#lem: galanzu[wise]; unkin[assembly]; imria[clan]; gal[big]; ri[impose]
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. dim₂-ma ma-da nu-ub-da-kur₂-ra na degₓ(RI) mu-un-e
#tr.en: I have been advised that the attitude (?) of the province has not altered.
#lem: dimma[thought]; mada[land]; kur[different]; na[cvne]; deg[gather up]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. ud lu₂-kiŋ₂-gi₄-a-ŋu₁₀ igi-zu-še₃ mu-e-ši-gi₄-a-ŋu₁₀
#tr.en: At the time I sent my messenger to you,
#lem: ud[sun]; kiŋgia[messenger]; igi[eye]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. egir-ra-ni-ta (1:{m}lu₂-{d}nanna:1) ensi₂ ma-da zi-mu-dar-ra{ki}-še₃
#tr.en: I sent another messenger, after him,
#lem: egir[back]; Lunanna[1]PN; ensik[ruler]; mada[land]; Zimudar[1]GN
#etcsl: line-id=28

:28v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) lu₂-{d}en-ki
#lem: Luenki[1]PN

29. lu₂-kiŋ₂-gi₄-a mu-ni-gi₄
#tr.en: to @varh[t3115.v5]{@wPN{Lu-@wDN{Nanna}} } @vart[t3115.v6,t3115.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} @wPN{Lu-@wDN{Enki}} }, the ruler of the province of @wGN{Zimudar}.
#lem: kiŋgia[messenger]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. 7200 erin₂ mu-e-ši-in-gi₄
#tr.en: He has sent you 7200 workers.
#lem: n; erin[people]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. lu₂ {gi}dusu ib₂-si lu₂ {ŋiš}tukul sag₃-ge bi₂-ib-tur
#tr.en: Basket men are available; however,
#lem: lu[person]; dupsik[basket (for carrying earth and bricks)]; si[fill]; lu[person]; tukul[weapon]; sag[strike]; tur[small]
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. tukum-bi lugal-ŋu₁₀ erin₂ kiŋ₂ ak-de₃ du₈-u₃-bi ab-be₂
#tr.en: men fit to engage in military action are limited. If my lord should arrange the dismissal of the workers ready to work,
#lem: tukumbi[if]; lugal[king]; erin[people]; kiŋ[work]; ak[do]; du[spread]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. u₃-šub {ŋiš}tukul ga-an-da-sag₃
#tr.en: let me pursue military action together with them, when I have removed (?) them.
#lem: ušub[brick-mold]; tukul[weapon]; sag[strike]
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. lu₂ gal-gal ma-da-za lu₂ in-ne-ši-in-gi₄
#tr.en: The dignitaries of your provinces are sending a man to them.
#lem: lu[person]; gal[big]; mada[land]; lu[person]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. igi-ne-ne ma-an-ŋar-re-eš-ma
#tr.en: They have presented themselves before me, announcing: @q[dignitaries,Carrum-bani]{“As far as we are concerned,
#lem: igi[eye]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. me-en-de₃ iri-iri en-nu-uŋ₃ nu-mu-da-ak-en-de₃-en
#tr.en: we are unable to guard all the cities.
#lem: menden[we]; iri[city]; ennuŋ[watch]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. a-na-gin₇-nam ugnim a-ra-ab-šum₂-mu
#tr.en: But how exactly will any troops be given to you?”}
#lem: anagin[how?]; ugnim[army]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. lu₂-kiŋ₂-gi₄-a-ŋu₁₀ mu-na-ni-in-gi₄-eš
#tr.en: My messenger has been sent to them (?).
#lem: kiŋgia[messenger]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. ud lugal-ŋu₁₀ a₂ mu-e-da-aŋ₂-ta
#tr.en: Once my lord has given me instructions, I will repeatedly return to (?) work at nightfall and at midnight, as well as engaging in military action.
#lem: ud[sun]; lugal[king]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. ud ten ŋi₆-ba kiŋ₂ im-mi-ib-gi₄-gi₄-in u₃ {ŋiš}tukul i₃-sag₃-ge-en
#tr.en: I stand at the disposal of the fame and word of my lord, and so I (?) will bring weapons to bear.
#lem: ud[sun]; ten[extinguish]; ŋi[night]; kiŋ[work]; gi[turn]; u[and]; tukul[weapon]; sag[strike]
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. mu inim lugal-ŋa₂-ke₄ i₃-gub-be₂-en {ŋiš}tukul ib₂-lah₄-lah₄-e
#tr.en: No strength has yet been displayed (?), nor any firmness shown (?) by means of weapons.
#lem: mu[name]; inim[word]; lugal[king]; gub[stand]; tukul[weapon]; lah[plural stem of tum ⟦bring⟧]
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. usu nu-um-ŋar {ŋiš}tukul-ta nu-um-me-ge-en ud kur-kur he₂-en-dul
#tr.en: Let the storm cover (?) all the lands!
#lem: usu[strength]; ŋar[put]; tukul[weapon]; gin[confirm]; ud[storm]; kur[mountain(s)]; dul[cover]
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. lugal-ŋu₁₀ he₂-en-zu
#tr.en: May my lord know!
#lem: lugal[king]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=43







